course: dictionary
lesson: 8500
title: Sapphire: a gem and a colour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a thing or describe a thing. «Sapphire» is a noun when it names a precious stone, and an adjective when it describes a colour, like «sapphire eyes» or «a sapphire sea». The words around it show you which one you are reading.
explain: Context clues help. A «sapphire ring» is a ring with a sapphire stone in it, and «sapphire blue» tells you the colour. Swap in another colour, such as «a grey sea», and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, sapphire is working as a colour word.
explain: Some sentences tell you facts about the word. «Rubies and sapphires are the same mineral, corundum; red corundum is ruby, and other colours are sapphire.» So a ruby is a red sapphire, and the colour is what makes the difference.
fact: A sapphire is a precious stone, usually a clear, deep blue, used in jewellery.
fact: «Sapphire» can also be an adjective for a bright, deep blue colour, as in «a sapphire sea».
fact: Sapphires can be pink, yellow or other colours, but red ones are called rubies.
fact: Sapphires are very hard, harder than most things except diamond.
fact: A «sapphire wedding anniversary» is the celebration after 45 years of marriage.
exercise: «The queen wore a sapphire ring at the party.» What is a sapphire in this sentence? | *A precious stone used in jewellery | A type of boat | A kind of fish | A loud musical instrument
exercise: «The sapphire sea sparkled under the sun.» What does sapphire describe here? | The sound of the waves | The name of a ship | *The colour of the sea | The size of the sea
exercise: Sapphires can be pink or yellow, but which colour is never called a sapphire? | Pink | *Red | Yellow | Green
test: «Rubies and sapphires are the same mineral, corundum; red corundum is ruby, and other colours are sapphire.» What does this tell you about a ruby? | It is a colour that is not found in nature | It is a kind of blue rock, not a stone | *It is red corundum, the same mineral as sapphire | It is a type of wood
test: «Rubies and sapphires are one mineral, corundum, and a pinch of another element decides the colour.» What decides the colour of these stones? | The shape it is cut into | Light from the sun | *A pinch of another element | The size of the stone
exam: Sapphire is very hard, harder than most things except which? | Gold | Glass | Wood | *Diamond
